# Testing

- Every bug fix gets a test that fails before the fix and passes after.
- Every new behaviour gets at least one happy-path and one edge/error-case test.
- Test behaviour through the public interface, not implementation details or private functions.
- Never delete, skip (`.skip`, `xit`, `@pytest.mark.skip`) or loosen assertions to make tests pass. If a test seems wrong, explain why and ask.
- Use the project's existing framework (Vitest/Jest/Playwright/pytest). Don't introduce a new one.
- Keep tests deterministic: no real network calls, fixed clocks and seeds, isolated temp dirs and databases.
- Name tests as sentences: `it("returns 404 when the post does not exist")`.
- Run the relevant tests after every change and report the actual output.
